    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="0952" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Frankfurt <hi rendition="#small-caps">USPolAd</hi>
                    Files—800 Germany</note>
                <head>No. 850<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of Political Affairs, United
                        States Group, Control Council, Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Heath</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Political Adviser in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>?], <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-17">July 17, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>Attached is the memorandum which you directed the Division<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d850-f1"/> to prepare on “Problems with which we are or may be
                    confronted in the US Zone and in Germany as a whole”. I don’t think the paper is
                    in the Division’s best vein. Some of the problems mentioned are small or are on
                    their way to solution and some of the policy guidance asked for in the
                    memorandum will be supplied as a result of the Conference, at least if the
                    American thesis is accepted.</p>
                <p>I have tried my hand at a new document, a rough draft of which is attached for
                    your consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Don</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ald
                            R. Heath</hi>]</signed></closer>





                <xi:include href="d850-a1.xml" xpointer="d850-a1"/>
